": "Anesthesia basics and positioning risks"}, {"id": "a3f72988-30a3-425d-ae48-e15123833c0c", "type": "concept", "title": "Specimen, count, and safety processes"}]}, {"id": "317bc2d1-777c-4bb6-bb96-99256fc7dc36", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Postoperative care", "description": "Post-op nursing centers on early detection and prevention of complications.", "children": [{"id": "4d8b7b9e-b72e-4381-99e4-1333c75eb027", "type": "concept", "title": "Airway, breathing, circulation, pain, and neuro checks"}, {"id": "cf1b4af9-6a54-49d5-ad21-719f249e4b5e", "type": "concept", "title": "Wound, drain, and dressing assessment"}, {"id": "d0a3d5c4-bd78-44a1-a08c-c19ff6fcd5cf", "type": "concept", "title": "DVT, atelectasis, ileus, infection, and mobility prevention"}]}]}, {"id": "6a256e12-d9de-43e3-910d-163ef8bcd2b7", "type": "topic", "title": "Pain Management and Comfort Care", "description": "Students learn to assess pain, plan multimodal interventions, monitor safety, and advocate for patient comfort.", "children": [{"id": "4565ec6a-1fdf-43f2-bbad-0e4dad32a63a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pain assessment", "description": "Pain care begins with systematic, individualized assessment.", "children": [{"id": "8e1a0907-74a7-4e1f-8449-8066c5db40be", "type": "concept", "title": "Numeric and functional pain scales"}, {"id": "bc01ae8c-cc9e-41b8-8b97-6471181bd6ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Acute, chronic, neuropathic, and procedural pain"}, {"id": "1a22fa40-8eca-4a62-af61-7a93facc7e1d", "type": "concept", "title": "Reassessment after intervention"}]}, {"id": "5432aa64-421f-4d20-be71-97b3bdd9ddf8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pharmacologic pain care", "description": "Students learn benefits, risks, and nursing responsibilities for analgesics.", "children": [{"id": "f89c2525-4121-446b-acee-7020513ab3c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Non-opioids, opioids, adjuvants, and regional approaches"}, {"id": "81f38e19-fd5b-41fe-a8c3-d16ca377a6df", "type": "concept", "title": "Sedation and respiratory monitoring"}, {"id": "d2fd1de0-7b1a-4391-88da-f4052737eaa5", "type": "concept", "title": "Bowel regimen, fall risk, and adverse effects"}]}, {"id": "480ac7e0-e7d1-4526-9d54-d3b85cbc09bc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nonpharmacologic comfort", "description": "Comfort care includes more than medication administration.", "children": [{"id": "dc6c20df-f43b-4c65-a645-72abe6c59609", "type": "concept", "title": "Positioning, heat/cold where appropriate, relaxation, and distraction"}, {"id": "b41d3e29-224e-4f35-8d8f-dd8399e8f634", "type": "concept", "title": "Sleep, anxiety, and environmental factors"}, {"id": "74b0dbde-cd16-4c84-8612-e2a401593065", "type": "concept", "title": "Trauma-informed and culturally responsive comfort measures"}]}]}, {"id": "c1649065-f3a3-493f-aa1c-938736964fa0", "type": "topic", "title": "Fluid, Electrolyte, and Acid-Base Balance", "description": "This module builds the physiologic and nursing foundation for recognizing and responding to common imbalances.", "children": [{"id": "204f9184-b3c3-4925-b8ed-850f5865350c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fluid balance", "description": "Students learn how volume status shapes perfusion, oxygenation, and renal function.", "children": [{"id": "a41c873f-309e-4e18-b8cc-9072fdb8f88b", "type": "concept", "title": "Intake/output and daily weights"}, {"id": "a2f7ed0f-6b9b-4cce-8773-7101ea6ab54d", "type": "concept", "title": "Hypovolemia and fluid overload"}, {"id": "599f66ce-a8a2-460a-9255-d8ca456b974c", "type": "concept", "title": "IV fluids and nursing monitoring"}]}, {"id": "4a04eada-fc9b-4577-b323-ce986a032aa2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Electrolyte disorders", "description": "Electrolytes are high-yield because they change heart, muscle, and neurologic function.", "children": [{"id": "a56f6e8d-fd54-4164-bd37-82dba98387a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Sodium, potassium, calcium, magnesium, and phosphate"}, {"id": "4b5c89a1-0320-4404-9df3-41cd3725d01a", "type": "concept", "title": "ECG and neuromuscular implications"}, {"id": "56a6b4f5-4533-4d9c-8f98-9a02eb62117b", "type": "concept", "title": "Replacement, restrictions, and safety checks"}]}, {"id": "a1e48865-db85-4724-a04e-d87fe23c5c54", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Acid-base interpretation", "description": "Basic acid-base reasoning helps students recognize respiratory and metabolic instability.", "children": [{"id": "de773c3f-7cb2-4a4e-86a4-fb835acf74d2", "type": "concept", "title": "ABG/VBG basics"}, {"id": "e3ee0d7b-41b8-4543-a2f9-af1c486462c9", "type": "concept", "title": "Respiratory acidosis/alkalosis"}, {"id": "855cbfe5-8e09-4da2-b027-ea66d32bd546", "type": "concept", "title": "Metabolic acidosis/alkalosis and compensation"}]}]}, {"id": "8114fdbe-4a70-4aaf-9ae0-4132494b9718", "type": "topic", "title": "Respiratory Disorders: Asthma, COPD, Pneumonia, and Oxygenation", "description": "Students learn assessment and nursing care for common respiratory disorders and impaired gas exchange.", "children": [{"id": "ecd007f8-447a-4616-8a41-2ec14706fb1d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Respiratory assessment", "description": "Students learn to recognize impaired oxygenation early.", "children": [{"id": "84fb1eeb-b046-4ee3-a647-71b12a0d3850", "type": "concept", "title": "Breath sounds, work of breathing, cough, sputum, and chest pain"}, {"id": "f29eb353-b317-4bfd-87c5-569e324abec8", "type": "concept", "title": "Pulse oximetry and oxygen delivery devices"}, {"id": "ceed2268-c91f-46c7-9e78-f6c6af4e2976", "type": "concept", "title": "Signs of respiratory distress and failure"}]}, {"id": "889d32a9-ba4e-4d89-9533-40e2f2eb4797", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Common disorders", "description": "The focus is nursing care for high-frequency adult respiratory conditions.", "children": [{"id": "2fe8dfe8-bc84-4de8-a949-c8f76f512dc1", "type": "concept", "title": "Asthma exacerbation"}, {"id": "39cfae99-0152-4f82-ba1f-ee6cb24514b6", "type": "concept", "title": "COPD and chronic bronchitis/emphysema"}, {"id": "d2aac830-4d94-49b7-b8cf-1b2b39c14898", "type": "concept", "title": "Pneumonia and aspiration risk"}]}, {"id": "ea402865-218d-4d7f-a5e7-4e21c9b89544", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interventions and teaching", "description": "Respiratory care blends medication, airway clearance, mobility, and education.", "children": [{"id": "c7f80e17-afa5-4291-aecb-34b6daf1e79d", "type": "concept", "title": "Bronchodilators, corticosteroids, antibiotics, and inhaler teaching"}, {"id": "261d80e4-f99d-4278-80e1-479721515443", "type": "concept", "title": "Incentive spirometry, coughing, deep breathing, and positioning"}, {"id": "c0254659-190d-4824-b730-67b3b4af4d38", "type": "concept", "title": "Smoking cessation, vaccines, and home oxygen safety"}]}]}, {"id": "e64b887c-0f7a-4f9b-b768-e8144ccb823d", "type": "topic", "title": "Cardiac Disorders: Coronary Artery Disease, Heart Failure, and Dysrhythmias", "description": "This topic introduces adult cardiac pathophysiology, monitoring, medications, and nursing priorities.", "children": [{"id": "1e841d0d-61dc-4acc-a0b9-ab44562d30ad", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cardiac assessment", "description": "Students learn to connect symptoms, vital signs, labs, and ECG monitoring to cardiac risk.", "children": [{"id": "d4d8dd88-1948-4df6-8301-6e4b08a66395", "type": "concept", "title": "Chest pain assessment"}, {"id": "d2a176ab-a675-4b8d-b50b-f0772f8dfd2b", "type": "concept", "title": "Perfusion, edema, lung sounds, and weight trends"}, {"id": "ad53efda-ab7d-4150-bcac-efe3aa540083", "type": "concept", "title": "Troponin, BNP, electrolytes, and basic ECG awareness"}]}, {"id": "d7fefe3e-961f-4108-9fa5-6482493d9a31", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Common cardiac conditions", "description": "This section builds foundational care for frequent adult cardiac diagnoses.", "children": [{"id": "0813b447-5f4c-4fb0-9e1f-4d3861283c2a", "type": "concept", "title": "Coronary artery disease and acute coronary syndrome"}, {"id": "8db347cf-d6b1-4547-9f36-9382914c553d", "type": "concept", "title": "Heart failure exacerbation"}, {"id": "42da98fc-d300-48ae-abcf-d070832c3e81", "type": "concept", "title": "Atrial fibrillation and common dysrhythmia concepts"}]}, {"id": "0efb4f85-a1b4-4ca7-ad89-93908c0b7b39", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nursing management", "description": "Students learn monitoring, medications, safety, and teaching priorities.", "children": [{"id": "38099d51-30f0-4f6b-b6d4-a3c799074dbe", "type": "concept", "title": "Oxygen, activity pacing, and symptom monitoring"}, {"id": "e152d11f-d5c2-4bfc-b87e-f05eb49b56fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Antiplatelets, anticoagulants, beta blockers, ACE inhibitors, diuretics, and nitrates"}, {"id": "1b19ee45-d140-4eb1-afa6-336f56c05dc1", "type": "concept", "title": "Diet, fluid/sodium, daily weights, and when to seek help"}]}]}, {"id": "0830ae40-4000-4cd2-926f-78f4ab08b0d7", "type": "topic", "title": "Vascular Disorders and Hypertension", "description": "Students learn care for vascular perfusion problems, hypertension, thromboembolic risk, and related patient teaching.", "children": [{"id": "598a6d1c-38d2-4f85-87f4-97cc4ac8f9b6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hypertension care", "description": "Hypertension is a core chronic condition with acute and long-term implications.", "children": [{"id": "07b974f8-cff6-4cfa-b3d3-4022901f02e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary and secondary hypertension"}, {"id": "55d453d5-aab8-42f1-8ff9-2f4f9c82d7fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Lifestyle, medication adherence, and home BP monitoring"}, {"id": "bbcd2eb5-bb9f-4a2a-b41c-1e3e36da5063", "type": "concept", "title": "Hypertensive urgency/emergency recognition"}]}, {"id": "42bf3f66-297a-41bb-8771-2afa0f739608", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Peripheral vascular disorders", "description": "Students learn to assess and support arterial and venous circulation.", "children": [{"id": "5a4f0374-3e5e-43a3-93fa-1a99a9f88d67", "type": "concept", "title": "Peripheral arterial disease"}, {"id": "5cc2a948-7adc-4c82-87