ctures, sprains, and casts"}, {"id": "4f3927fd-edfc-4b01-92df-db55ed81afb1", "type": "concept", "title": "Osteoarthritis, osteoporosis, and back pain"}, {"id": "b16330e6-7ddf-4ca0-93b5-708e5b07ccab", "type": "concept", "title": "Postoperative joint replacement basics"}]}, {"id": "74ad7a86-ab10-42c7-807c-4110587e108e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rehabilitation-oriented nursing", "description": "Med-surg nurses help patients regain function safely.", "children": [{"id": "eb57a8d5-e747-44ba-b8ef-052d09810f22", "type": "concept", "title": "Early mobility and collaboration with PT/OT"}, {"id": "fc5a9af7-f4a7-43eb-be5d-a84b5b0a7d89", "type": "concept", "title": "Pain control for participation"}, {"id": "3a51feeb-2361-4047-a08d-60fd2350e882", "type": "concept", "title": "Home safety, assistive devices, and prevention teaching"}]}]}, {"id": "03da4956-dd35-4b80-b7c3-198fc363f48b", "type": "topic", "title": "Diagnostics, Laboratory Interpretation, and Medication Implications", "description": "Students learn to connect diagnostics and medications to nursing assessment, patient safety, and teaching.", "children": [{"id": "0c6decd6-60e3-4d1d-8eff-c14ce86c5ec5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diagnostic procedures", "description": "Students learn how nurses prepare, monitor, and teach around common tests.", "children": [{"id": "fd523f70-a233-4ddc-96ea-889497cf33d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Imaging and contrast precautions"}, {"id": "3cf9d825-5871-4781-94ef-4c941a811503", "type": "concept", "title": "Endoscopy, cardiac tests, pulmonary tests, and glucose testing"}, {"id": "84dd5ef3-2bce-4ad6-9a40-96859b946708", "type": "concept", "title": "Pre- and post-procedure nursing responsibilities"}]}, {"id": "2599177d-2918-483d-a046-719a6d8e251b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Laboratory interpretation", "description": "The aim is not diagnosis alone but nursing action based on trends and risk.", "children": [{"id": "b0df5a76-7a75-4ee9-9d95-e4e2b56ca538", "type": "concept", "title": "CBC, CMP, coagulation studies, cardiac markers, ABGs, and urinalysis"}, {"id": "4d5147be-b380-49f8-924a-d8af933d9e51", "type": "concept", "title": "Critical values and escalation"}, {"id": "c8b84780-d5bc-4a4e-a777-9cb26ec1aa07", "type": "concept", "title": "Trend interpretation and clinical context"}]}, {"id": "03b27876-1416-4bbb-b449-7ba2570d84c1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Medication implications", "description": "Medication knowledge becomes real in med-surg when tied to disease, labs, and patient teaching.", "children": [{"id": "61ded7ce-b8e4-4f20-8f9c-740b0c756123", "type": "concept", "title": "Medication reconciliation"}, {"id": "da2329be-2dba-4cd6-88eb-8f51c38b799e", "type": "concept", "title": "High-alert medications and adverse effects"}, {"id": "dd41314a-2757-4d1c-a1f8-cd7be41aad99", "type": "concept", "title": "Patient education and teach-back"}]}]}, {"id": "65d80739-e2ee-404c-8e5a-f07af507e98a", "type": "topic", "title": "Clinical Judgment for Deterioration, Delegation, and Complex Adult Care", "description": "This module builds early-recognition, prioritization, delegation, and rapid-response thinking for worsening adult patients.", "children": [{"id": "bf50d8ef-fbde-44da-9512-87ff2da8c669", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Recognizing deterioration", "description": "Students learn early cues that an adult patient is becoming unstable.", "children": [{"id": "ca3305da-ea63-4378-af65-6dd22a4dc1cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Changes in mental status, work of breathing, perfusion, urine output, and vital signs"}, {"id": "f37d642c-d16c-49fb-a36f-c7ada909cc1b", "type": "concept", "title": "Sepsis and shock warning signs"}, {"id": "1df9dec1-7bf0-4e46-b0cd-09c7a7a8971b", "type": "concept", "title": "Rapid response triggers"}]}, {"id": "3b02c303-da81-4c91-a885-a8f32e200dd1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Prioritization and delegation", "description": "Safe care requires knowing what the RN must do and what can be delegated.", "children": [{"id": "fb53e4a3-